        "Abstract": "This paper describes the construction of a large Japanese web corpus for training large language models (LLMs). The corpus was created by extracting and refining text from the Common Crawl archive, resulting in approximately 312.1 billion characters. The quality of the corpus was confirmed through continual pre-training experiments on various LLMs, showing consistent improvements on Japanese benchmark datasets."
